#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-radio-v1.rst:7
#: 85ae1394b582475da1ccb42ddf277b0b
msgid "This article explains how to connect the *3DR Radio v1* to your flight controller. You should also read :ref:`SiK Radio v2 <common-sik-telemetry-radio>`, which contains a more detailed user guide and feature list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-radio-v1.rst:17
#: f38c135958df4459a79c229b52a1fda9
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-radio-v1.rst:19
#: d72e3b415eac4be2b590011a59ea2bf4
msgid "The *3DR Radio* is the easiest way to setup a telemetry connection between your autopilot and a ground station."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-radio-v1.rst:22
#: 41fc2c381b934f96b0c4ca545303a59a
msgid "There are two versions of the 3DR Radio (version 2 is more recent, see link above). The radios have slightly different form factors and connections (v2 comes with a built-in FTDI cable) but otherwise their behaviour is very similar."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-radio-v1.rst:30
#: f2ee213e0d9d4e7fb996e220d298b55e
msgid "."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-radio-v1.rst:32
#: 6866fb8c2dd9475486676589c9d69c68
msgid "This article only covers the main difference between the two radios — connecting the radios."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-radio-v1.rst:36
#: 976dedd346424b64ae2bde4f31b2777d
msgid "Connecting the radio"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-radio-v1.rst:38
#: a5ca4de400e243eeb28e3b300d089fed
msgid "3DR Radio v1 has different radio modules for air and ground:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-radio-v1.rst:40
#: c99eb1ba36234c74bdef973daa4b7970
msgid "The \"ground\" module has a USB connector making it easy to connect directly to your ground station. On a windows 7 or higher machine, the require drivers should be automatically installed the first time you plug in the ground module but if it does not install for some reason or the ground computer is running Windows XP (or earlier) you can get the D2XX FTDI driver `here. <http://www.ftdichip.com/Drivers/D2XX.htm>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-radio-v1.rst:47
#: fd044c55a2a04ece946def95995519f4
msgid "The 'aircraft' module has a FTDI six pin header, allowing it to be directly connected to your Autopilot's telemetry port as shown in the following sections."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-radio-v1.rst:53
#: 07f8ca240fec40659735f8c07a4f4b03
msgid "Connecting to the AutoPilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-radio-v1.rst:55
#: 0e6efd2478884f1fbcaa9bd9d36d3782
msgid "The aircraft module will be need to be connected to an autopilot's serial port, sometimes marked as TELEM1 or TELEM2. The TX and RX pins of the radio to the RX and TX signals of the Serial port. If the port has CTS and RTS pins, then connecting them will provide flow control and increased reliability at longer ranges. The ``SERIALx_PROTOCOL`` for the UART port to which the module is connected should be set to \"2\" (MAVLink2).Be sure that the radio is programmed with the latest firmware in order to work properly with MAVLink2 protocol. See the section below for programming."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-radio-v1.rst:61
#: 601542e45fda49c19eec58c7f128b8f1
msgid "Changing Configuration of the Radio"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-radio-v1.rst:63
#: 76bf3aeee42d4e4caba09f22e2e38cce
msgid "This is not usually required, but if desired see: :ref:`common-configuring-a-telemetry-radio-using-mission-planner`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-radio-v1.rst:68
#: 62bde4828479471bb1e2cacab37d0623
msgid "Updating the Firmware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-radio-v1.rst:70
#: b8e68e17e2524ef38bf82f869ffa05b2
msgid "Using Mission Planner, with the module connected to the autopilot for power and the base USB unit plugged into the computer:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-radio-v1.rst:72
#: 82304210113648b78d385c1ab7f97c23
msgid "determine the USB COMM port the base radio is using and enter that into the port selection box of Mission Planner along with the baud rate (57600 is default for the radios)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-radio-v1.rst:73
#: 4acf95a24dfd44e68f7fb5c05fd12ebf
msgid "WITHOUT connecting anything in Mission Planner, use the SETUP/Optional Hardware/Sik Radio utility tab to \"Upload Firmware (local)\" which will download the latest firmware and write it to the radios."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-radio-v1.rst:74
#: dae38d4b6e3f496ea23f3d9a170290f0
msgid "You may now CONNECT to the base radio COMM port with Mission Planner over MAVLink using the radio links."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-radio-v1.rst:75
#: 8825178a99614aa7a3188c4e84bdc45a
msgid "If you have any problems, be sure that the autopilot's SERIAL port connected to the radio is set to the baud rate (57600 default) and the protocol is MAVLink2 (\"2\")"
msgstr ""
